comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T21:25:57.770Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: complete all-status strict read covered 2593 readable items with no omissions. Closed pm-6sc8jq owns truthful stale-lifecycle governance for external blockers while pm-p9sc owns local dangling projections and pm-uxkf owns edge-aware blocked reads. No open item owns re-resolution plus safe validation classification. This recurrence is canonical for GitHub 1146 and 1147."
  "2026-08-28T21:26:39.465Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage evidence: issues #1146 and #1147 both point to this canonical combined external-blocker lifecycle and validation item at its merge-stable main-branch toon path."
  "2026-08-28T23:24:21.263Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: external classification, graph, actionability, next, and validation regressions passed; packed Node and Bun SDK consumers imported the public classifier successfully; full coverage passed exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-29T00:14:46.009Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence: linked acceptance passed 9/9; the complete repository suite passed 586/586 files and 8100/8100 tests; exact coverage passed 60114/60114 statements, 45310/45310 branches, 12497/12497 functions, and 57886/57886 lines; repository static quality, command grammar, MCP parity, defect evidence, duplication, docs links, secret scan, and packed npm+Bun acceptance all passed."
  "2026-08-29T02:22:15.295Z","harness:codex","Review-round evidence: external locators preserve provider-specific case, structured locators become graph nodes even without source_kind, and stale resolver disposers cannot delete a replacement registration. The actionability, graph, validation, resolver, packed Node SDK, and packed Bun SDK paths pass."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T23:24:37.448Z","harness:codex","A syntactically valid remote locator is a typed graph node even when no resolver is installed. Unknown external state must remain explicit evidence, never be rewritten as local dangling corruption."
  "2026-08-29T00:14:46.442Z","harness:codex","Provider integrations belong behind the SDK resolver registry: core classifies and preserves external identity while bounded package-owned providers supply lifecycle evidence. Resolver failures and absent providers fail closed to explicit unknown state instead of deleting context."
